### doctor
$ hermes lastprice doctor
Last Price doctor
  seller model: openai/gpt-4o-mini on openrouter (Hermes's own model: deal chats and both duel sellers use it)
  buyer (duel, bench): runs on your own model (openai/gpt-4o-mini); model override: NOT granted.
    To let `--buyer MODEL` pick another model, run `hermes plugins enable last-price` in an interactive terminal and answer y.
  free path: an OpenRouter key with no credit runs `:free` models. Seller: `hermes config set model.default google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`; buyer: `--buyer google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`. Free models are rate-limited, so a duel can stall; on the Hermes desktop app's Nous free tier, the seller runs on `nous/welcome`.
  state: readable · 1 item(s) · shop open · C:\Users\Dflame\.hj4\plugin-data\agent-plugin-last-price-80cd1435\state.json (3 KB of 10240 KB)
  ledger: c:\users\dflame\.hj4\plugin-data\agent-plugin-last-price-80cd1435\ledger.jsonl (3 turns, 1 sale; `hermes lastprice report` counts the same)
  hosts contacted: openrouter.ai (your model provider: buyer messages, drafts, rewrites). Nothing else: no telemetry, no payment provider.
  owners: local terminal only
  shop platforms: none (duels only)
  What leaves this machine:
    - buyer messages and Hermes's draft replies go to your model provider (as in any Hermes chat);
    - a rewrite of a too-low draft goes to the same model through ctx.llm: it sees the buyer's message,
      the draft and the current counter, never the floor;
    - in a duel, the buyer's instruction and the seller's replies go to the buyer model you name;
    - in a duel with --vs-prompt and in every bench, the STOCK seller gets the duel item's floor written
      into its system prompt, which goes to your model provider: by default that is the demo item's
      throwaway floor, never one of your items unless you pass --item <id> --real-item;
    - nothing else: no telemetry, no payment calls yet (pay links are placeholders in 0.1.x).
  Tools and processes:
    - Deal sessions (the Last Price seller, and buyers' chats) may use only Last Price's three tools, plus Hermes's tool-search bridge (`tool_search`, `tool_describe`, `tool_call`): Hermes resolves a `tool_call` to the real tool before `pre_tool_call` sees it, so a call through the bridge is checked like any other; `tool_search` and `tool_describe` only read the session's tool catalog.
    - The stock seller runs with Hermes's `todo` toolset plus every plugin toolset your profile turns on by default (Last Price's own three tools answer "not active" there).
    - `duel` and `bench` run `hermes chat` child processes, never with `--yolo`, with `--ignore-rules` (your AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, .cursorrules, memory and preloaded skills stay out, so both sellers start from the same prompt) and `--source tool` (the duel sessions stay out of your session list).
    - `challenge start` (Telegram) changes six Hermes settings through `hermes config set`: TELEGRAM_ALLOW_ALL_USERS, platform_toolsets.telegram, platforms.telegram.extra.allow_admin_from, platforms.telegram.extra.user_allowed_commands, platforms.telegram.extra.group_allow_admin_from, platforms.telegram.extra.group_user_allowed_commands. It saves their earlier values first, and `challenge end` restores each one (a key that was not set before is unset again).
  What stays here: floors, stops and salts in plugin state under your Hermes home; the deal ledger (JSONL).
    The floor is hidden from the model in deal sessions, which cannot read files. On your own machine it is your data, stored as plain JSON in plugin state: readable by you and by any agent you give file tools to.
